modernc.org/sqlite needs modernc.org/libc, which has no linux/sparc64
port. Leave the driver out on sparc64.

The RPM cataloger refuses to run without a driver, which fails every
scan. Warn instead, as syft 1.18 did. SQLite rpmdbs are then skipped
and the Nix cataloger logs an error for a Nix store database.

diff --git a/cmd/syft/main.go b/cmd/syft/main.go
--- a/cmd/syft/main.go
+++ b/cmd/syft/main.go
@@ -1,8 +1,6 @@
 package main
 
 import (
-	_ "modernc.org/sqlite"
-
 	"github.com/anchore/clio"
 	"github.com/anchore/syft/cmd/syft/cli"
 	"github.com/anchore/syft/cmd/syft/internal"
diff --git a/cmd/syft/sqlite.go b/cmd/syft/sqlite.go
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/cmd/syft/sqlite.go
@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
